    "narrative": "With the Zurich Zebras navigating a light schedule today, the heavy lifting falls on **Junior Caminero**, who anchors the lineup with a Strong 72.77 efficiency score. Facing Shawn Armstrong, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a favorable 4.35 xERA matchup and a projected promotion to the three-hole, which optimizes his counting stat potential. While his base projection sits at 60.68, the current recency bias and the premium placed on his platoon advantage against right-handed pitching push him into must-start territory. With our elite speed threats like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Josh Smith** all off today due to scheduling gaps, we lack our usual stolen base floor, making the run production from **Junior Caminero** essential to keeping our weekly Roto pace competitive.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant today as the core roster of **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** all face team off-days, forcing the optimizer to essentially pivot toward a skeleton crew. **Carson Benge** and **Lars Nootbaar** were considered for utility spots, but their projected efficiency failed to clear the 40-point threshold required to warrant burning a game cap. We are essentially playing a defensive configuration, protecting our remaining games-played allowance until our full contingent\u2014including **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014returns to the diamond. Monitor the lineup card for **Junior Caminero** closely; if he slides out of the #3 spot, his efficiency score will be docked accordingly, though he remains the only viable anchor for today's limited slate.",
